# 📚 Linked List (Part 1) - Introduction to Linked Lists

## 📌 Introduction

A **Linked List** is a linear data structure in which elements are stored in separate memory locations and connected using pointers (or references).

Unlike arrays, linked lists do **not require contiguous memory**, making insertion and deletion operations much more efficient.

Linked Lists are widely used in:

- Dynamic Memory Allocation
- Stacks & Queues
- Graphs
- Hash Tables
- Browser History
- Music Playlists
- Operating Systems

